Z||000000||wardog85GT||10-29-2001||08:16 PM|||| Has any one ever tried to install a flowmaster muffler designed for a 3rd gen. camaro on a fiero? They look very similar due to single inlet, dual outlet configuration.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||10-29-2001||09:54 PM||||I got one. You'll probably have a hard time getting a "real" shop to put it on for you, as there are no brackets to put the supports on. However, I have had mine hanging from just the tailpipe hangers for about 25000 miles / 3 years, no problems.<BR>And yeah, it does sound cool.  There are other good options out there, but if you want a Flowie, it will work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-29-2001||11:33 PM||||I do know that it's almost a perfect fit on 84-87 V6s.  I planned on putting it on my 88, but found it wouldn't fit on the 88s (DOH).  I've got one for sale for a killer deal, check it out in the mall:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005446.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum4/HTML/005446.html</A> <P>Most any competent exhaust person will figure out the rubber mounts, they're not hard.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||10-30-2001||01:52 AM||||I have one tooooo... sound's REALLY AGGRESIVE...    Steve  *The Smoooooth One*...||||reg||1
Z||000004||watts||10-30-2001||02:45 AM||||Can anyone describe the difference between the 88 and pre 88 mounts that make them not work?<P>I've got an '88 setup sitting here, and I can't see the difference from my buddies '85.<P>What am I missing?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric_PA||10-30-2001||05:40 AM||||I have one on my Fiero..it's a tight fit and a lot of custom work. I installed it with a 3800 this week. It sounds great! I will have pics soon.<BR>||||reg||1
